# Shell scripts must keep LF line endings on every checkout: a CRLF
# post-install script does not run (`\r` becomes part of each command), and
# a Windows checkout converts them unless told otherwise (core.autocrlf).
# The other text files are kept LF too, so the checks in
# packaging/packaging_test.go read the same bytes on every OS.
* text=auto eol=lf
